      "description": "Cream serif display on deep wine, copper italic emphasis, copper accent rule at top.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-hero\"><div class=\"ds-rule\"></div><h1 class=\"ds-hero-t\">Where Faith Meets <em>Rigorous Scholarship</em></h1><p class=\"ds-hero-s\">An interdisciplinary graduate school in Toronto and online.</p></section>",
      "css": ":host{--wine:#9B0D24;--wine-deep:#7A0A1C;--wine-mid:#BE0B28;--wine-soft:#D44B5E;--accent:#A85A32;--accent-light:#C87A52;--accent-muted:#8E4A28;--accent-pale:#EEDACA;--accent-deep:#7A4020;--teal:#7A5C3A;--teal-muted:#6B4E30;--teal-pale:#E6D9C6;--teal-deep:#5A4228;--cream:#FDFBF7;--cream-warm:#F9F5ED;--text-dark:#2E1318;--text-body:#3A3330;--text-on-dark:#E8C2C2;--border-light:rgba(155,13,36,0.08);--serif:'Libre Baskerville',Georgia,serif;--sans:'Outfit',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,sans-serif;--ease:cubic-bezier(0.25,0.46,0.45,0.94);} .ds-hero{position:relative;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(122,10,28,0.98),rgba(122,10,28,0.85));padding:3rem 2rem;} .ds-rule{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--accent),var(--accent-light) 40%,transparent 80%);} .ds-hero-t{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.4rem);font-weight:700;color:var(--cream);line-height:1.12;margin:0 0 1.1rem;} .ds-hero-t em{font-style:italic;color:var(--accent-light);} .ds-hero-s{font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:300;font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-on-dark);max-width:560px;margin:0;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Footer",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "site-footer",
      "description": "Wine-deep footer: serif brand, copper uppercase headings, rose-mist links.",
      "html": "<footer class=\"ds-foot\"><div class=\"ds-foot-brand\">Institute for Christian Studies</div><div class=\"ds-foot-h\">Programs</div><a class=\"ds-foot-a\" href=\"#\">Master of Arts</a><a class=\"ds-foot-a\" href=\"#\">PhD</a></footer>",
      "css": ":host{--wine:#9B0D24;--wine-deep:#7A0A1C;--wine-mid:#BE0B28;--wine-soft:#D44B5E;--accent:#A85A32;--accent-light:#C87A52;--accent-muted:#8E4A28;--accent-pale:#EEDACA;--accent-deep:#7A4020;--teal:#7A5C3A;--teal-muted:#6B4E30;--teal-pale:#E6D9C6;--teal-deep:#5A4228;--cream:#FDFBF7;--cream-warm:#F9F5ED;--text-dark:#2E1318;--text-body:#3A3330;--text-on-dark:#E8C2C2;--border-light:rgba(155,13,36,0.08);--serif:'Libre Baskerville',Georgia,serif;--sans:'Outfit',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,sans-serif;--ease:cubic-bezier(0.25,0.46,0.45,0.94);} .ds-foot{background:var(--wine-deep);color:var(--text-on-dark);padding:2.5rem 2rem;font-family:var(--sans);border-top:1px solid rgba(168,90,50,0.12);} .ds-foot-brand{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--cream);margin-bottom:1.2rem;} .ds-foot-h{font-size:0.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent-light);margin-bottom:0.8rem;} .ds-foot-a{display:block;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-on-dark);text-decoration:none;padding:0.15rem 0;transition:color 0.2s ease;} .ds-foot-a:hover,.ds-foot-a:focus-visible{color:var(--accent-light);outline:none;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Business Card (front / back)",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "business-card-front",
      "description": "Print extension: call on the cream front, response on the wine back, tone-on-tone dove. Screen approximation of the 3.5 x 2 in card; print values are CMYK.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-cards\"><div class=\"ds-card ds-front\"><div class=\"ds-call\">a tradition of inquiry,</div><div class=\"ds-name\">Edith van der Boom</div><div class=\"ds-cred\">PhD</div><div class=\"ds-tl\">Director, Educational Leadership</div><div class=\"ds-hair\"></div><div class=\"ds-em\">evanderboom@icscanada.edu</div><div class=\"ds-tl\">416-979-2331</div><div class=\"ds-web\">icscanada.edu</div><div class=\"ds-logo\">ICS</div></div><div class=\"ds-card ds-back\"><svg class=\"ds-dove\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"50\"/></svg><div class=\"ds-resp\">a spirit of<br>engagement.</div><div class=\"ds-sig\"><b>Institute for Christian Studies</b><br><span>59 St. George Street, Toronto ON  M5S 2E6</span></div></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--wine:#9B0D24;--wine-deep:#7A0A1C;--wine-mid:#BE0B28;--wine-soft:#D44B5E;--accent:#A85A32;--accent-light:#C87A52;--accent-muted:#8E4A28;--accent-pale:#EEDACA;--accent-deep:#7A4020;--teal:#7A5C3A;--teal-muted:#6B4E30;--teal-pale:#E6D9C6;--teal-deep:#5A4228;--cream:#FDFBF7;--cream-warm:#F9F5ED;--text-dark:#2E1318;--text-body:#3A3330;--text-on-dark:#E8C2C2;--border-light:rgba(155,13,36,0.08);--serif:'Libre Baskerville',Georgia,serif;--sans:'Outfit',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,sans-serif;--ease:cubic-bezier(0.25,0.46,0.45,0.94);} .ds-cards{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;} .ds-card{position:relative;overflow:hidden;width:350px;height:200px;box-sizing:border-box;padding:18px;font-family:var(--sans);} .ds-front{background:var(--cream);} .ds-back{background:var(--wine);} .ds-call{font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:12px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;} .ds-name{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:21px;color:var(--wine);line-height:1.1;} .ds-cred{font-size:9px;color:var(--accent-muted);margin:2px 0 6px;} .ds-tl{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:300;color:var(--text-dark);line-height:1.3;} .ds-hair{width:31px;height:0;border-top:0.7px solid var(--accent);margin:8px 0 6px;} .ds-em{font-size:10.3px;color:var(--wine);} .ds-web{font-size:10.3px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.02em;color:var(--accent);} .ds-logo{position:absolute;right:18px;bottom:20px;font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:700;font-size:30px;color:var(--wine-mid);} .ds-dove{position:absolute;width:278px;height:278px;right:-67px;top:-39px;fill:#86091D;} .ds-resp{position:relative;font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;color:var(--cream);} .ds-sig{position:absolute;left:18px;bottom:16px;font-size:10px;color:var(--cream);line-height:1.35;} .ds-sig b{font-weight:500;} .ds-sig span{color:var(--text-on-dark);font-size:9.4px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Scholar's Hearth",
    "overview": "A warm, bookish world. Wine and cream set the ground, copper carries the voice, and a warm umber gives programs a second register. Libre Baskerville carries what the institution says: names, headings, and an italic speaking voice. Outfit carries the facts: dates, contacts, labels, body copy. Surfaces are flat and square-cornered. Depth comes from tone (wine over wine-deep, cream over cream-warm), with a soft lift on hover.\n\nThe website (`css/styles.css` plus per-page CSS) is the source of the world. Print is an extension of it. The business card (`info/BusinessCards/make_ics_card.py`) carries the same palette in CMYK, the same two faces, and the same copper thread, compressed to 3.5 × 2 in.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Wine-drenched heroes and footers; cream content grounds.",
      "Copper for the italic voice, calls to act, and thin rules.",
      "Serif for what is said, sans for what is stated.",
      "Square buttons and cards, with small radii only on tags.",
      "Tone-on-tone depth rather than heavy shadow."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Copper Voice Rule",
        "body": "Copper speaks: italic phrases, calls to act and rules. Wine names. Never set a name or heading in copper, and never set the italic voice in wine.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Logo Red Rule",
        "body": "On print, brand red (#BE0B28) appears only in the logo, on cream. On wine, the logo reverses to cream. It is never set in copper, umber or ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Baskerville for what is said (names, headings, the italic voice), Outfit for what is stated (contacts, dates, labels, body). Don't swap them.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Six-Point Floor Rule",
        "body": "No print text below 6 pt. A line that cannot fit at its floor is refused and must be rewritten, not shrunk further.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lift-On-Hover Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces rest flat. On hover they rise 1–3px with a soft tinted shadow, and touch devices drop the lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the logo intact, drawn from `SVG-Logos/` vectors: brand red on cream, cream on wine.",
      "Do keep the dove watermark tone-on-tone (one step darker, +10K) so text can cross it and stay legible.",
      "Do set print colour in CMYK from the table above. Confirm brand red with the printer before a large run.",
      "Do keep copper to the voice, actions and rules, and let wine and cream carry the mass.",
      "Do hold print type at or above its floor (6 pt minimum, 12 pt for names)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't set the whole tagline on one face of the card. The split is the card's idea.",
      "Don't extract, crop or restyle any part of the logo except the dove \"C\" watermark, and don't use the watermark in a contrasting colour.",
      "Don't round buttons or cards.",
      "Don't introduce cool hues. The palette is wine, copper, umber and cream; the only exception is a third-party mark in its own colour, such as the Facebook widget's blue."
    ]
  }
}